From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:14:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(l10n): Spanish for upstream's hardcoded literals and its
 weak translations

Tools/victor_l10n.py runs after `git am` (CI) and, locally, before a build:
- Tools/victor_l10n/{settings,screens,dates}.json: exact find -> replace rules
  that route ~1,380 hardcoded English UI literals through our own resources
  (res/values{,-es}/strings_victor_l10n_*.xml) and show month/day names in
  the phone's language. A rule whose text upstream changed is skipped, so the
  patch queue never conflicts with upstream's own i18n work.
- Tools/victor_l10n/es_fixes.json: 790 corrected Spanish strings (tuteo,
  "pulsera", leftovers in English, garbled machine translation). Written to
  the `full` flavor overlay only while upstream's English still matches.
- The Paper/Porcelain light-style labels now come from resources.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
